# Formatting scope: Prettier owns source and configuration in this repository,
# not the written blueprint.
#
# printWidth 80 matches the prose in the existing Markdown line for line, but
# Prettier's Markdown printer additionally pads every table cell so the columns
# line up. Running it would rewrite every table in the root documents, docs/,
# and docs/decisions/ (14 files) and produce a large diff against the reviewed
# first commit that says nothing about formatting quality. Some of the padded
# tables come out well over 80 columns, so this is not a printWidth that can be
# tuned into agreement. Whether the documents adopt Prettier is a decision for
# whoever owns them, and it belongs in its own commit.
**/*.md

# specs/ is the pinned machine-readable source snapshot
# (docs/STANDARDS_REGISTRY.md). Prettier reflows its inline sequences and JSON
# arrays; a formatting pass must never show up in the diff of a pinned spec.
/specs/
